 v4 | 6.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-032 | substation-a | v4 | 7.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-033 | substation-b | v4 | 9.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-034 | generator-1 | v4 | 7.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-035 | fuel-yard | v4 | 8.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-036 | substation-a | v4 | 6.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-037 | substation-b | v4 | 8.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-038 | generator-1 | v4 | 9.4 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-039 | fuel-yard | v4 | 7.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-040 | substation-a | v4 | 8.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-041 | substation-b | v4 | 7.1 | megawatts | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSeparate rated, usable, generated, and reserved power with exact durations.\nName current tests for transfer, load shedding, fuel replenishment, and rollback.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"source_path\":\"sources/FALCON_TREATMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\",\"source_size_bytes\":3344,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Treatment barriers, disinfectant, and turbidity controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU. The release gate is at or below 0.30 NTU for four hours; 0.18 NTU is not a chlorine residual.\nFree chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution. Entry and distribution thresholds are different controls.\nFilter media, coagulant dose, source-water blend, contact time, or UV configuration changes stale prior treatment verification.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGARNET source-water findings set FALCON treatment assumptions. BASTION residence time and CIPHER sampling determine whether treated water evidence applies downstream.\nDELTA demand ramps cannot outrun FALCON verified capacity or required disinfectant contact time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| TRT-000 | clarifier | v2 | 0.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-001 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-002 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-003 | uv-train | v2 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-004 | clarifier | v2 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-005 | filter-bank | v2 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-006 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-007 | uv-train | v2 | 3.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-008 | clarifier | v2 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-009 | filter-bank | v2 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-010 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-011 | uv-train | v2 | 2.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-012 | clarifier | v2 | 0.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-013 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-014 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 2.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-015 | uv-train | v3 | 1.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-016 | clarifier | v3 | 2.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-017 | filter-bank | v3 | 0.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-018 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 1.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-019 | uv-train | v3 | 3.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-020 | clarifier | v3 | 1.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-021 | filter-bank | v3 | 2.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-022 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 0.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-023 | uv-train | v3 | 2.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-024 | clarifier | v3 | 0.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-025 | filter-bank | v3 | 1.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-026 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 3.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-027 | uv-train | v3 | 1.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-028 | clarifier | v4 | 2.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-029 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-030 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 2.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-031 | uv-train | v4 | 0.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-032 | clarifier | v4 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-033 | filter-bank | v4 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-034 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-035 | uv-train | v4 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-036 | clarifier | v4 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-037 | filter-bank | v4 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-038 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 3.1 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-039 | uv-train | v4 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-040 | clarifier | v4 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-041 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve NTU, mg/L, locations, duration, and barrier dependencies.\nState pause, rollback, and evidence needed to retire temporary treatment controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GARNET:1-64+HELIX:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"031d750e445931a9a1ff5df2226522f79babe80df9a5261f0a43ab6f7e8f4fc8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7462}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GARNET_SOURCE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3622,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Source-water contamination hypotheses and watershed controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe ash-plume model assigns a 34 percent chance of intake impact during the next rain event. That is a forecast probability, not 34 percent measured contamination.\nObserved volatile-organic screening is non-detect at the reservoir and 3.1 micrograms per liter at the river intake. The two locations must not be merged.\nThe investigation hold remains active for the chemical yard because the containment trench has not been inspected below grade.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nFALCON treatment selection depends on GARNET source hypotheses; CIPHER must sample each materially different source path.\nJASPER governs environmental notifications, while AURORA retains restoration and public-health authority separation.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SRC-000 | river-intake | v2 | 3.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-001 | reservoir | v2 | 4.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-002 | ash-plume | v2 | 6.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-003 | chemical-yard | v2 | 4.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-004 | river-intake | v2 | 5.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-005 | reservoir | v2 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-006 | ash-plume | v2 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-007 | chemical-yard | v2 | 6.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-008 | river-intake | v2 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-009 | reservoir | v2 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-010 | ash-plume | v2 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-011 | chemical-yard | v2 | 5.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-012 | river-intake | v2 | 3.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-013 | reservoir | v2 | 4.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-014 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-015 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-016 | river-intake | v3 | 5.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-017 | reservoir | v3 | 3.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-018 | ash-plume | v3 | 5.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-019 | chemical-yard | v3 | 6.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-020 | river-intake | v3 | 4.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-021 | reservoir | v3 | 5.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-022 | ash-plume | v3 | 4.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-023 | chemical-yard | v3 | 5.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-024 | river-intake | v3 | 3.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-025 | reservoir | v3 | 4.9 | ri